From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the present BH runs on the main loop thread only

What: the IOSurface present's bottom half (cocoa_gl_present_bh, which draws
the newest frame after a display-link tick) is created on the iohandler
AioContext instead of qemu_bh_new's main context.

Why: qemu_bh_new's context is also run by a vCPU thread that waits in
AIO_WAIT_WHILE (a block drain from the guest's NVMe reset, say). That BH
blits with GL and reads virglrenderer's scanout texture, so it could run
GL and virgl on a vCPU thread. With every virgl user holding the BQL that
was harmless; with virgl running without the BQL
(qemu-virtio-gpu-virgl-unlocked.patch) it would race. Upstream moved
virtio-gpu's own BHs to the iohandler context for the same reason
(235f9b36, "virtio-gpu: Ensure BHs are invoked only from main-loop thread").

Upstream: OmacVM only (the present code is ours).
Test: build-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh checks the call; src/tests/gpu-unlocked.sh.

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
index 9f4df1e..1756313 100644
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -7077,7 +7077,14 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_init(void)
     present_input_first = present_vsync && in && !strcmp(in, "1");
     present_nsurf = present_vsync ? PRESENT_SURFACES : 3;
     if (present_vsync) {
-        present_bh = qemu_bh_new(cocoa_gl_present_bh, NULL);
+        /*
+         * OmacVM: on the iohandler context, which only the main loop thread
+         * runs. qemu_bh_new's context is also run by a vCPU waiting in
+         * AIO_WAIT_WHILE (a block drain), and this BH draws with GL and reads
+         * virgl's textures: one thread for virgl, as virtio-gpu's own BHs.
+         */
+        present_bh = aio_bh_new(iohandler_get_aio_context(),
+                                cocoa_gl_present_bh, NULL);
     }
     info_report("cocoa: frames shown %s",
                 !present_vsync ? "when drawn" :
